  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "HarborLogi 작업 관제",
    "overview": "The implemented workbench carries the existing HarborLogi navy, teal, orange and ivory identity into a Korean operation interface. Dense task facts sit on quiet surfaces; the current task and next check receive the clearest emphasis.\n\nThe local read-only interface separates Harbor business state, ROSY execution and physical receipt evidence. Demo data is visibly identified. This document records the implementation, not production authentication, field usability acceptance or physical device acceptance.",
    "keyCharacteristics": ["Persistent brand header and adjacent task list.","Separate business, execution and evidence sections.","Text labels accompany state colors."],
    "rules": [],
    "dos": ["Do keep business state, ROSY execution and receipt evidence separately labeled.","Do pair status color with readable text and preserve keyboard focus.","Do reuse the existing Harbor name, container H icon and concept banner."],
    "donts": ["Don't present demo data or concept artwork as device evidence.","Don't imply that a read, an Action success or a receipt authorizes execution or completes all business checks.","Don't present this local workbench as production login, RBAC or physical acceptance."]
